xpertise and logistics capabilities. It also provides a range of MRO products in the rotating equipment, bearing, power transmission, hose, fluid power, metal working, fastener, industrial supply, safety products, and safety services categories. This segment serves customers in the oil and gas, general industrial, manufacturing, chemical, food and beverage, refining, water and wastewater, fabrication and construction, and other industries. Its Supply Chain Services segment manages procurement and inventory optimization and management, store-room management, transaction consolidation and control, vendor oversight and procurement cost optimization, productivity improvement, and customized reporting services. The company's programs include SmartAgreement, a procurement solution for various MRO categories; SmartBuy, an on-site or centralized MRO procurement solution; SmartSource, an on-site procurement and storeroom management solution; SmartStore, an e-Catalog solution; SmartVend, an industrial dispensing solution; and SmartServ, an integrated service pump solution. The Innovative Pumping Solutions segment fabricates and assembles custom-made pump packages; remanufactures pumps; and manufactures branded private label pumps. The company was formerly known as INDEX INC and changed its name to DXP Enterprises, Inc. in May 1997. DXP Enterprises, Inc. was founded in 1908 and is based in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. Little | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 73 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $614K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["DXP Enterprises, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.2B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $54M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.06\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.009969581304803745},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2801108.78},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Comparison: Capstone Therapeutics (NASDAQ:CAPS) vs. DXP Enterprises (NASDAQ:DXPE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/financial-comparison-capstone-therapeutics-nasdaqcaps-vs-dxp-enterprises-nasdaqdxpe.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793963713.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is DXP Enterprises (DXPE) Undervalued As Its Earnings Miss Clouds The Q4 Outlook?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dxp-enterprises-dxpe-undervalued-earnings-101807181.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793960287.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"DXPE Q3 2026 deep dive: margin pressures emerge despite double-digit sales growth","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/dxpe/news/earnings-call/dxpe-q3-2026-deep-dive-margin-pressures-emerge-despite-double-digit-sales-growth","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793944370.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.54,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"DXP (DXPE) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/dxp-dxpe-q3-2026-earnings-204742000.html","date